    "seconds": 52,
    "summary": "The ad service was failing every request because of a feature-flag default, and I've reverted that default. All pods are Running and the ad service is serving requests again.\n\n**Root cause:** The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `adFailure` set to `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`, which makes the ad service fail every request. The upstream default is `\"off\"`. The `ad` and `flagd` deployments were restarted at <time> just before the problem appeared, but I didn't find out who changed the ConfigMap or whether that restart was involved.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- Set `adFailure.defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap in `astronomy-shop`. Nothing else in the file changed.\n- Restarted `deploy/flagd` so its init container re-copied the corrected config. The rollout completed successfully.\n\n**Verification:** The ad logs show targeted ad requests (for example `[telescopes]`, `[travel]`) succeeding after the change. No pods are in a non-ready state.\n\n**Caveat:** This is a Helm-managed release, so a future `helm upgrade` could reapply the chart's flag values and reintroduce the problem if the override came from there. The durable fix would be in the Helm values, which I didn't have access to here. I haven't made any git commits.",
    "timed_out": false,
